mes>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schepers</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Koopman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phylogeny of the SOX family of developmental transcription factors based on sequence and structural indicators</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>227</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11071752</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kishi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mizuseki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasai</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamazaki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiota</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakanishi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Requirement of Sox2-mediated signaling for differentiation of early Xenopus neuroectoderm</article-title><source>Development</source><year>2000</year><volume>127</volume><fpage>791</fpage><lpage>800</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10648237</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Sandberg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kallstrom</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Muhr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sox21 promotes the progression of vertebrate neurogenesis</article-title><source>Nat Neurosci</source><year>2005</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>995</fpage><lpage>1001</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15995704</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></n